  <div class="wrap">
<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Distinguishing genuine liabilities from genuine equity</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 37 governs the PRESENTATION of FINANCIAL instruments â€” MOST notably, the CLASSIFICATION of an ISSUED instrument as a FINANCIAL LIABILITY or as EQUITY, based on ITS substance RATHER than its LEGAL form. THE Standard also governs OFFSETTING of financial ASSETS and LIABILITIES. IT works ALONGSIDE ASBE No. 22 (classification and MEASUREMENT) to FORM the COMPLETE financial INSTRUMENTS framework, CLOSELY converged with IAS 32 internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Issued financial instruments and offsetting</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to the PRESENTATION and CLASSIFICATION of FINANCIAL instruments an ENTERPRISE ISSUES, and the CIRCUMSTANCES under WHICH financial ASSETS and LIABILITIES may be OFFSET against EACH other.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Liability/Equity Classification Test</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A contractual obligation to deliver cash or another financial asset</div><div class="principle">AN issued INSTRUMENT is CLASSIFIED as a FINANCIAL LIABILITY WHERE the ISSUER has a CONTRACTUAL obligation to DELIVER cash or ANOTHER financial ASSET to the HOLDER, or to EXCHANGE financial INSTRUMENTS under POTENTIALLY unfavourable CONDITIONS. ABSENT such an OBLIGATION, the INSTRUMENT is CLASSIFIED as EQUITY â€” CONSISTENT with IAS 32'S own substance-OVER-form classification TEST internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Compound Financial Instruments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Splitting a convertible bond into its liability and equity components</div><div class="principle">A "COMPOUND" instrument â€” SUCH as a CONVERTIBLE bond, COMBINING a LIABILITY component (the BOND obligation) and an EQUITY component (the HOLDER'S conversion OPTION) â€” is SPLIT at INITIAL recognition, WITH each COMPONENT presented SEPARATELY according to ITS own substance.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Puttable Instruments â€” a Narrow Equity Exception</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Certain puttable instruments may still qualify as equity</div><div class="principle">CERTAIN "PUTTABLE" instruments (GIVING the HOLDER the RIGHT to PUT the instrument BACK to the ISSUER for cash) MAY still be CLASSIFIED as EQUITY, PROVIDED they MEET specific, NARROW criteria (e.g. ENTITLING the HOLDER to a PRO RATA share of NET assets on LIQUIDATION, and BEING the MOST SUBORDINATE class of instrument) â€” a NARROW exception CONSISTENT with IAS 32'S OWN puttable-instrument EXCEPTION internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Offsetting Financial Assets and Liabilities</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Two conditions must both be met</div><div class="principle">A FINANCIAL asset and a FINANCIAL liability are OFFSET (presented as a SINGLE net AMOUNT) ONLY WHERE the ENTITY has a CURRENTLY enforceable LEGAL right to SET OFF the recognised AMOUNTS, AND intends EITHER to SETTLE on a NET basis or to REALISE the asset and SETTLE the liability SIMULTANEOUSLY â€” BOTH conditions must be MET.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Treasury Shares</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Deducted from equity, no gain or loss on subsequent transactions</div><div class="principle">WHERE an ENTERPRISE reacquires ITS own equity INSTRUMENTS (TREASURY shares), THEY are DEDUCTED directly FROM equity â€” WITH NO gain or LOSS recognised in PROFIT or loss on the PURCHASE, sale, ISSUE, or CANCELLATION of an ENTITY'S own equity INSTRUMENTS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example â€” Classifying a Convertible Bond's Components</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Splitting proceeds between liability and equity</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A convertible bond issuance</div><div class="wk-body">A company issues a convertible bond for RMB 100,000,000. A similar bond without the conversion feature would have a fair value of RMB 92,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company allocates RMB 92,000,000 to the LIABILITY component (the STRAIGHT bond OBLIGATION), and the REMAINING RMB 100,000,000 âˆ’ RMB 92,000,000 = <strong>RMB 8,000,000</strong> to the EQUITY component (the CONVERSION option), presented SEPARATELY within OWNERS' equity.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example â€” Applying the Offsetting Criteria</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Both conditions must be met to present a net figure</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A receivable and payable with the same counterparty</div><div class="wk-body">A company has a RMB 5,000,000 receivable and a RMB 3,000,000 payable with the same counterparty, with a legally enforceable master netting agreement in place, and both parties intend to settle net.</div><div class="wk-answer">Since BOTH conditions are MET (LEGAL right to SET OFF, and INTENTION to SETTLE net), the company presents a SINGLE net RECEIVABLE of RMB 5,000,000 âˆ’ RMB 3,000,000 = <strong>RMB 2,000,000</strong>, RATHER than the TWO gross amounts SEPARATELY.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 37 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Classification basis for compound and puttable financial instruments</span><span>Amounts of financial assets and liabilities offset in the Balance Sheet, and the related enforceable rights</span><span>Treasury shares held, and movements during the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Classifying an instrument as a liability, equity, or a compound combination of both</span><span>Whether the offsetting criteria are genuinely met</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of a straight (non-convertible) bond, underlying compound instrument splitting</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 32</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison â€” ASBE 37 vs IAS 32</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 37</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 32</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Liability/equity classification test</span><span>Substance over form</span><span>Substance over form â€” converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Offsetting criteria</span><span>Legal right + intention to settle net</span><span>Legal right + intention to settle net â€” converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard, MIRRORING IAS 32 CLOSELY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every financial instrument presentation event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Compound instrument split</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bo">SCOE</span></span><span>Liability and equity components presented separately</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 22</span><span>Recognition and Measurement of Financial Instruments â€” supplies the classification and measurement rules this Standard's presentation requirements build upon</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Compound financial instrument</div><div class="glossary-def">An instrument combining both a liability component and an equity component, such as a convertible bond, split and presented separately.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Treasury shares</div><div class="glossary-def">An enterprise's own equity instruments it has reacquired, deducted directly from equity with no gain or loss recognised.</div></div>
</div>
</div>
